#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286679 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7874d3c1-1e7d-5935-918f-98a39cbf1ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286681} {:answer/id #uuid "15d53ce7-5bf9-5cbc-801d-aca9e585a89b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6s^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7874d3c1-1e7d-5935-918f-98a39cbf1ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286681} :answer-field/id #uuid "a76f6768-6175-5831-9bef-cf3c3433a53d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef0e7ebd-8eb3-5e6b-8197-77c0558d373a" :question/math-academy-id "q-313364" :question/problem "The volume of a right square pyramid is increasing. Given that its height $h$ is always twice the length of a base, find the rate of change of the volume of the pyramid with respect to its base length $s.$\n\n*Hint*: The volume of a right square pyramid is $V=\\frac{1}{3}{s}^{2}h.$ \n\nThe rate of change of the pyramid’s volume with respect to $s$ is \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given that $h=2s,$ so we can express the volume of the pyramid $V$ as a function of the base edge length $s$ by substituting $h=2s$ in the formula of the volume. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(s) & =\\frac{1}{3}{s}^{2}h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{s}^{2}(2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{s}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $V(s)$ with respect to $s$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{d}{ds}\\,(\\frac{2}{3}{s}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{d}{ds}\\,({s}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{s}^{2} \\\\  & =2{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the rate of change of the pyramid’s volume with respect to its base length $s$ is $2{s}^{2}.$"}]}
